ough AL. Borrowed time. Philadelphy: Temple University Press; 1986. [ Google Scholar ] Koenig BA. In: Biomedicine examined. Lock M, Gordon DR, editor. Dordrecht: Kluwer Academic Publishers; 1988. The technological imperative in medical practice: the social creation of a "routine" treatment; pp. 465–496. [ Google Scholar ] Kumar N. Victory for girl told she was too young to have a lung transplant, The independent. London, England; 2013. http://www.independent.co.uk/life-style/health-and-families/health-news/victory-for-girl-told-she-was-too-young-to-have-a-lung-transplant-8658228.html . [ Google Scholar ] Sharp LA. Organ transplantation as a transformative experience: anthropological insights into the restructuring of the self. Medical Anthropol Q. 1995;9(3):357–389. doi: 10.1525/maq.1995.9.3.02a00050. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Kierans C, Kierans C. In: Culture, bodies and the sociology of health. Surrey EE, editor. England: Ashgate; 2010. Transplantation, organ donation and (in)human experience: Re-writing boundaries through embodied perspectives on kidney failure; pp. 21–44. [ Google Scholar ] Aims and scope. http://www.blackwellpublishing.com/aims.asp?ref=1600-6135&site=1 . About the journal. http://journals.lww.com/transplantjournal/pages/aboutthejournal.aspx . Svenaeus F. Organ transplantation and personal identity: how does loss and change of organs affect the self? J Med Philos. 2012;37:139–158. doi: 10.1093/jmp/jhs011. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Kierans C. Narrating kidney disease: the significance of sensation and time in the emplotment of patient experience. Culture Med Psychiatry. 2005;29:341–359. doi: 10.1007/s11013-005-9171-8. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Seale C. Media and health. London: Sage; 2002. [ Google Scholar ] Hammer R. In: Donner, recevoir un organe Droit, dû, devoir. Thiel M-J, editor. Strasbourg: Presses Universitaires de Strasbourg; 2009. Le traitement médiatique de la pénurie et du don d’organes: variations 