Liu G. Point‐of‐care ultrasound in internal medicine: establishing standards for Europe. Eur J Intern Med 2020; 75: 28–29. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 21. Ma IWY, Steinmetz P, Weerdenburg K, Woo MY, Olszynski P, Heslop CL et al . The Canadian medical student ultrasound curriculum: a statement from the Canadian ultrasound consensus for undergraduate medical education group. J Ultrasound Med 2020; 39: 1279–1287. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 22. Thompson C. General and acute medicine in Australasian hospitals. Future Hosp J 2016; 3: 65–67. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 23. Bhagra A, Tierney DM, Sekiguchi H, Soni NJ. Point‐of‐care ultrasonography for primary care physicians and general internists. Mayo Clin Proc 2016; 91: 1811–1827. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 24. Johannessen O, Uthaug Reite F, Bhatnagar R, Ovrebotten T, Einvik G, Myhre PL. Lung ultrasound to assess pulmonary congestion in patients with acute exacerbation of COPD. Int J Chron Obstruct Pulmon Dis 2023; 18: 693–703. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 25. Lichtenstein D, Meziere G. A lung ultrasound sign allowing bedside distinction between pulmonary edema and COPD: the comet‐tail artifact. Intensive Care Med 1998; 24: 1331–1334. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 26. Lichtenstein DA, Meziere GA. Relevance of lung ultrasound in the diagnosis of acute respiratory failure: the BLUE protocol. Chest 2008; 134: 117–125. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 27. Volpicelli G, Cardinale L, Garofalo G, Veltri A. Usefulness of lung ultrasound in the bedside distinction between pulmonary edema and exacerbation of COPD. Emerg Radiol 2008; 15: 145–151. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 28. Lammoza N, Murphy N, Evans N, Gibbs H, Elliott P. Point‐of‐care ultrasound: prime time has arrived. Intern Med J 2024; 54: 2089–2090. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 29. Peris A, Tutino L, Zagli G,