Carr PL, Friedman RH, Amos H, Ash AS, Moskowitz MA. Minority faculty and academic rank in medicine. Jama. 1998;280(9):767–771. doi: 10.1001/jama.280.9.767. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 33. National Resident Matching Program (NRMP). MATCH Communication Code of Conduct. 2019 http://www.nrmp.org/communication-code-of-conduct/ Accessed February 2020. 34. Alweis RL, Williams CM, Luther VP, et al. AAIM guidelines for interview and post-interview communication for graduate medical education recruitment. Am J Med. 2019;132(9):1106–1111. doi: 10.1016/j.amjmed.2019.05.023. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 35. Artinian NT, Drees BM, Glazer G, et al. Holistic admissions in the health professions: strategies for leaders. Coll Univ. 2017;92(2):65. [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 36. Grabowski CJ. Impact of holistic review on student interview pool diversity. Adv Health Sci Educ. 2018;23(3):487–498. doi: 10.1007/s10459-017-9807-9. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 37. Colford C, Kraemer MS, Contarino M, et al. After the match: cultivating a community of support, retention, and mentoring to enhance diversity. Am J Med. 2018;131(12):1520–1523. doi: 10.1016/j.amjmed.2018.07.029. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 38. Grbic D, Morrison E, Sondheimer HM, Conrad SS, Milem JF. The association between a holistic review in admissions workshop and the diversity of accepted applicants and students matriculating to medical school. Acad Med. 2019;94(3):396–403. doi: 10.1097/ACM.0000000000002446. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 39. Capers Q, IV, Clinchot D, McDougle L, Greenwald AG. Implicit racial bias in medical school admissions. Acad Med. 2017;92(3):365–369. doi: 10.1097/ACM.0000000000001388. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 40. DiBrito SR, Lopez CM, Jones C, Mathur A. Reducing implicit bias: association of women surgeons# HeForShe task force best practice recommendations. J Am Coll Surg. 2019;228(3):303–309. doi: 10.1016/j.jamcollsurg.2018