Med Sci. 1999;54:M370–M376. doi: 10.1093/gerona/54.7.m370. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 28. Matthews DA, McCullough ME, Larson DB, Koenig HG, Swyers JP, Milano MG. Religious commitment and health status: a review of the research and implications for family medicine. Arch Fam Med. 1998;7:118–124. doi: 10.1001/archfami.7.2.118. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 29. McBride JL, Arthur G, Brooks R, Pilkington L. The relationship between a patient''s spirituality and health experiences. Fam Med. 1998;30:122–126. [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 30. Kaldjian LC, Jekel JF, Friedland G. End-of-life decisions in HIV-positive patients: the role of spiritual beliefs. AIDS. 1998;12:103–107. doi: 10.1097/00002030-199801000-00012. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 31. Sloan RP, Bagiella E, Powell T. Religion, spirituality, and medicine. [see comments] Lancet. 1999;353:664–667. doi: 10.1016/s0140-6736(98)07376-0. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 32. Post SG, Puchalski CM, Larson DB. Physicians and patient spirituality: professional boundaries, competency, and ethics. Ann Intern Med. 2000;132:578–583. doi: 10.7326/0003-4819-132-7-200004040-00010. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 33. Asser SM, Swan R. Child fatalities from religion-motivated medical neglect. Pediatrics. 1998;101(part 1):625–629. doi: 10.1542/peds.101.4.625. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 34. Pargament KI, Koenig HG, Tarakeshwar N, Hahn J. Religious struggle as a predictor of mortality among medically ill elderly patients: a 2-year longitudinal study. Arch Intern Med. 2001;161:1881–1885. doi: 10.1001/archinte.161.15.1881. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 35. Koenig HG. Religion and medicine I: historical background and reasons for separation [see comments] Int J Psychiatry Med. 2000;30:385–398. doi: 10.2190/2RWB-3AE1-M1E5-TVHK. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 36. Sloan RP, Bagiella E, VandeCreek L, et al. Should physicians prescribe religious activities? N Engl J Med. 2000;34