171(6):612–614. doi: 10.1016/S0002-9610(97)89605-5. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 26. Ratanawongsa N, Thomas PA, Marinopoulos SS, et al. The reported validity and reliability of methods for evaluating continuing medical education: a systematic review. Acad Med. 2008;83(3):274–283. doi: 10.1097/ACM.0b013e3181637925. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 27. Tian J, Atkinson NL, Portnoy B, Gold RS. A systematic review of evaluation in formal continuing medical education. J Contin Educ Health Prof. 2007;27(1):16–27. doi: 10.1002/chp.89. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 28. Cook DA, Beckman TJ. Current concepts in validity and reliability for psychometric instruments: theory and application. Am J Med. 2006;119(2):166. doi: 10.1016/j.amjmed.2005.10.036. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 29. Messick S. Validity. In: Linn RL, editor. Educational Measurement. Phoenix, AZ: Onyx Press; 1993. [ Google Scholar ] 30. Messick S. Validity of psychological assessment: Validation of inferences from persons'' responses and performances as scientific inquiry into score meaning. Am Psychol. 1995;50(9):741–749. doi: 10.1037/0003-066X.50.9.741. [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 31. American Educational Research Association, American Psychological Association, National Council on Measurement in Education, Joint Committee on Standards for Educational and Psychological Testing (U.S.). Standards for Educational and Psychological Testing . Washington, DC: American Educational Research Association; 1999. 32. Downing SM. Validity: On meaningful interpretation of assessment data. Med Educ. 2003;37(9):830–837. doi: 10.1046/j.1365-2923.2003.01594.x. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 33. Beckman TJ, Cook DA, Mandrekar JN. What is the validity evidence for assessments of clinical teaching? J Gen Intern Med. 2005;20(12):1159–1164. doi: 10.1111/j.1525-1497.2005.0258.x. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 34. Asch DA, Jedrziewski MK, Christakis NA. Response rates to