ard: an ethnographic study. Med Teach 2016;38:793–800. 10.3109/0142159X.2015.1104411 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 20. Hammersley M, Atkinson P. Ethnography: principles in practice. 3rd edn London: Routledge; 2007. [ Google Scholar ] 21. Atkinson P. The clinical experience: the construction and reconstruction of medical reality. 2nd edn. Ashgate: Aldershot, 1997. [ Google Scholar ] 22. Patton M. Qualitative research & evaluation methods. London: SAGE, 2002. [ Google Scholar ] 23. Kvale S, Brinkmann S. Transcribing interviews. In InterViews: learning the craft of qualitative research interviewing. 2nd edn Los Angeles: Sage Publications, 2009. [ Google Scholar ] 24. LePine JA, LePine MA, Jackson CL. Challenge and hindrance stress: relationships with exhaustion, motivation to learn, and learning performance. J Appl Psychol 2004;89:883–91. 10.1037/0021-9010.89.5.883 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 25. Helmich E, Bolhuis S, Prins J et al. Emotional learning of undergraduate medical students in an early nursing attachment in a hospital or nursing home. Med Teach 2011;33:e593–601. 10.3109/0142159X.2011.610837 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 26. Kasman DL, Fryer-Edwards K, Braddock CH III. Educating for professionalism: trainees’ emotional experiences on IM and pediatrics inpatient wards. Acad Med 2003;78:730–41. 10.1097/00001888-200307000-00017 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 27. Levitt DS, Cooke M. Tips for teaching in longitudinal clerkships. Clin Teach 2011;8:93–6. 10.1111/j.1743-498X.2010.00420.x [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 28. Glouberman S, Zimmerman B. Complicated and complex systems: what would sucesssful reform of medicare look like? Toronto: University of Toronto Press Inc., 2004. [ Google Scholar ] 29. Dyche L, Epstein RM. Curiosity and medical education. Med Educ 2011;45:663–8. 10.1111/j.1365-2923.2011.03944.x [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 30. Dall''Alba G, Sandberg J. Unveiling professional development: a critical rev